---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Seed – B2B SaaS Financial Operations Platform — Dennis Essien"
  description="Designing an enterprise B2B financial workspace that transforms complex recurring billing, multi-currency invoicing, and ledger reconciliation into total clarity."
>
  <article class="project-detail">
    <div class="project-detail__inner">
      <a href="/work" class="project-detail__back">← Back to Work</a>

      <header class="project-detail__header">
        <div class="project-detail__tags">
          <span class="project-detail__tag"># Product Design</span>
          <span class="project-detail__tag"># B2B SaaS</span>
          <span class="project-detail__tag"># FinTech</span>
          <span class="project-detail__tag"># Design System</span>
        </div>

        <h1 class="project-detail__title">Seed</h1>
        <p class="project-detail__tagline">
          B2B SaaS financial operations platform — transforming high-density corporate billing, ledger reconciliation, and subscription scheduling into an effortless, scalable enterprise workspace.
        </p>

        <div class="project-detail__meta">
          <div class="project-detail__meta-item">
            <span class="project-detail__meta-label">Client</span>
            <span class="project-detail__meta-value">Seed Financial Systems</span>
          </div>
          <div class="project-detail__meta-item">
            <span class="project-detail__meta-label">Role / Scope</span>
            <span class="project-detail__meta-value">Lead Product & UX Architect</span>
          </div>
          <div class="project-detail__meta-item">
            <span class="project-detail__meta-label">Timeline</span>
            <span class="project-detail__meta-value">6 Weeks (2025)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="project-detail__meta-item">
            <span class="project-detail__meta-label">Domain</span>
            <span class="project-detail__meta-value">Enterprise B2B FinTech</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </header>

      <!-- Full-Width Hero Visual Showcase -->
      <div class="project-detail__hero-showcase">
        <img 
          src="/images/projects/seed.webp" 
          alt="Seed enterprise SaaS platform interface showcase overview"
          loading="eager"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </div>

      <!-- SECTION 1: PROJECT BRIEF -->
      <section class="project-detail__section">
        <div class="project-detail__section-grid">
          <aside class="project-detail__section-sidebar">
            <div class="project-detail__badge">
              <span>01 / Project Brief</span>
            </div>
          </aside>
          <div class="project-detail__section-body">
            <h2 class="project-detail__section-headline">
              Liberating enterprise finance teams from spreadsheet fragmentation and manual reconciliation.
            </h2>
            <p>
              Seed is a comprehensive B2B financial operating platform engineered to centralize complex billing schedules, customer invoicing ledgers, and cashflow reconciliation into a single unified source of truth. As subscription businesses scale from series-A to global enterprise operations, their financial data structures become astronomically complex—involving multi-currency settlements, usage-based metering, and tiered team authorizations.
            </p>
            <p>
              Our design engagement centered on turning high-density business intelligence into an ergonomic, low-friction workspace. Rather than masking complexity behind oversimplified consumer interfaces, we built tools that empower controllers, accountants, and revenue leaders to manage mission-critical billing data with speed, accuracy, and total peace of mind.
            </p>

            <div class="project-detail__cards-grid">
              <div class="project-detail__card">
                <h4>Primary Objective</h4>
                <p>Architect an enterprise workspace that accelerates monthly close cycles, reduces invoice dispute rates, and provides instant visibility into accounts receivable.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="project-detail__card">
                <h4>UX Methodology</h4>
                <p>Task-driven progressive disclosure, tabular numeric typography, contextual slide-out inspection drawers, and keyboard-first power workflows.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="project-detail__media-single">
          <img 
            src="/images/projects/seed/seed 3.webp" 
            alt="Seed Subscription Scheduling and Invoice Generation Interface"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <div class="project-detail__caption">Subscription Scheduling & Invoicing Architecture — Milestone Triggers, Auto-Retry Logic & Tax Compliance</div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SECTION 2: THE PROBLEM -->
      <section class="project-detail__section">
        <div class="project-detail__section-grid">
          <aside class="project-detail__section-sidebar">
            <div class="project-detail__badge project-detail__badge--alert">
              <span>02 / The Problem</span>
            </div>
          </aside>
          <div class="project-detail__section-body">
            <h2 class="project-detail__section-headline">
              Visual fatigue, disjointed audit trails, and catastrophic manual entry errors.
            </h2>
            <p>
              Interviews with corporate finance directors and controllers uncovered a persistent paradox: modern companies rely on modern tools for marketing and product development, yet their finance teams are trapped in legacy software resembling 1990s accounting databases. The consequences are severe: delayed revenue recognition, billing discrepancies, and employee burnout during quarterly closes.
            </p>
            <p>
              Core UX challenges identified during discovery:
            </p>

            <div class="project-detail__cards-grid">
              <div class="project-detail__card">
                <h4>Context Loss via Page Redirects</h4>
                <p>In legacy systems, clicking into a single transaction invoice navigates away from the master cashflow ledger, destroying filtered search states and forcing accountants to re-query their datasets hundreds of times daily.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="project-detail__card">
                <h4>Data Clutter & Numeric Illegibility</h4>
                <p>Generic proportional sans-serif fonts caused decimal misalignments across dense financial tables, increasing the risk of costly billing calculation blunders.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="project-detail__card">
                <h4>Insecure Team Permission Flows</h4>
                <p>All-or-nothing admin invites forced companies to grant full bank and payroll access to junior accounts receivable clerks merely so they could create invoices.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SECTION 3: THE SOLUTION & UX STRATEGY -->
      <section class="project-detail__section">
        <div class="project-detail__section-grid">
          <aside class="project-detail__section-sidebar">
            <div class="project-detail__badge project-detail__badge--success">
              <span>03 / The Solution</span>
            </div>
          </aside>
          <div class="project-detail__section-body">
            <h2 class="project-detail__section-headline">
              A modular drawer architecture, tabular design tokens, and role-based permissions matrix.
            </h2>
            <p>
              We established an ergonomic, high-density design system engineered around rapid keyboard navigation, zero-loss contextual exploration, and clear operational hierarchy:
            </p>

            <div class="project-detail__cards-grid">
              <div class="project-detail__card">
                <h4>Pillar 1: Zero-Loss Inspection Drawers</h4>
                <p>Auditing transaction receipts, customer credit histories, or payment methods occurs in a persistent right-hand drawer. The underlying ledger remains visible and active, eliminating navigation fatigue.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="project-detail__card">
                <h4>Pillar 2: Monospaced Tabular Typography</h4>
                <p>Configured precision typographic tokens featuring tabular figures, right-aligned monetary values, and semantic color-coded badges for payment statuses (Paid, Pending, Overdue, Disputed).</p>
              </div>
              <div class="project-detail__card">
                <h4>Pillar 3: Granular Role-Based Access Matrix</h4>
                <p>Designed a transparent permission provisioning system allowing managers to delegate billing, auditing, or reporting rights with complete security compliance.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- VISUAL GALLERY OF WORK -->
        <div class="project-detail__gallery-block">
          <div class="project-detail__gallery-grid project-detail__gallery-grid--2col">
            <div class="project-detail__gallery-item">
              <img src="/images/projects/seed/seed 4.webp" alt="Customer Ledger and Payment Records View" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <div class="project-detail__caption">Customer Ledger & Payment Records View — Multi-Tier Filter Architecture</div>
            </div>
            <div class="project-detail__gallery-item">
              <img src="/images/projects/seed/seed 5.webp" alt="Automated Recurring Billing Scheduler" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <div class="project-detail__caption">Automated Recurring Billing Scheduler & Timeline Milestones</div>
            </div>
            <div class="project-detail__gallery-item">
              <img src="/images/projects/seed/seed 6.webp" alt="Role-Based Team Permission Management" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <div class="project-detail__caption">Role-Based Team Permission Management & Access Delegation Matrix</div>
            </div>
            <div class="project-detail__gallery-item">
              <img src="/images/projects/seed/seed 7.webp" alt="Real-Time Revenue Analytics and Metrics" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <div class="project-detail__caption">Real-Time Revenue Analytics & Financial Performance Dashboard</div>
            </div>
            <div class="project-detail__gallery-item">
              <img src="/images/projects/seed/seed 8.webp" alt="Enterprise Invoicing Configuration Modal" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <div class="project-detail__caption">Enterprise Invoicing Configuration Modal & Custom Token Editor</div>
            </div>
            <div class="project-detail__gallery-item">
              <img src="/images/projects/seed/seed 9.webp" alt="Transaction Drill-Down Details Drawer" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <div class="project-detail__caption">Transaction Drill-Down Details Drawer with Complete Event Audit Log</div>
            </div>
            <div class="project-detail__gallery-item">
              <img src="/images/projects/seed/seed 10.webp" alt="Multi-Currency Settlement Flow" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <div class="project-detail__caption">Multi-Currency Settlement Flow & Automated Exchange Rate Reconciliation</div>
            </div>
            <div class="project-detail__gallery-item">
              <img src="/images/projects/seed/seed 1.jpeg" alt="Seed platform main invoicing interface" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <div class="project-detail__caption">High-Density Invoicing Hub & Batch Processing Surface</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="project-detail__media-single">
            <img 
              src="/images/projects/seed/seed 2.jpeg" 
              alt="Seed platform customer management and revenue timeline"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            />
            <div class="project-detail__caption">Customer Account Lifecycle & Aging Schedule — Predictive Cashflow Projections</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- SECTION 4: IMPACT & KEY OUTCOMES -->
      <section class="project-detail__section">
        <div class="project-detail__section-grid">
          <aside class="project-detail__section-sidebar">
            <div class="project-detail__badge">
              <span>04 / Impact</span>
            </div>
          </aside>
          <div class="project-detail__section-body">
            <h2 class="project-detail__section-headline">
              Radical time savings, zero billing discrepancies, and rapid enterprise adoption.
            </h2>
            <p>
              Following deployment across early enterprise cohorts, Seed reduced month-end closing times from days to hours while delivering unprecedented situational clarity to executive finance teams.
            </p>

            <div class="project-detail__metrics-row">
              <div class="project-detail__metric-box">
                <div class="metric-number">4.5x</div>
                <div class="metric-desc">Faster Invoice Creation & Dispatch Velocity</div>
              </div>
              <div class="project-detail__metric-box">
                <div class="metric-number">-65%</div>
                <div class="metric-desc">Reduction in Monthly Reconciliation Discrepancies</div>
              </div>
              <div class="project-detail__metric-box">
                <div class="metric-number">&lt; 1hr</div>
                <div class="metric-desc">New Finance Team Member Onboarding Ramp Time</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- PROJECT FOOTER NAVIGATION -->
      <nav class="project-detail__nav-footer" aria-label="Project pagination">
        <a href="/work/op1">← Previous: OP-1 Field Synthesizer</a>
        <a href="/work">All Selected Works</a>
        <a href="/work/xtoken">Next: xToken Terminal →</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
